  "_comment": "Lease scheduler vs the tuned baselines on W1 0.95X (282 tasks), seeds 42-44, 12 runs, ~3 h; each seed's four runs go back to back, so stopping early leaves complete sets. (1) fifo_c5: four slots, no host cache, the tuned fixed-concurrency baseline. (2) lease_p4: same server, one slot per task, held up to 2 s. (3) lease_p5: five slots, no host cache. (4) fifo_c6_p5_cram4g: the Phase 2 main line (five slots + 4 GiB host cache, FIFO c = 6), i.e. the fixed cache policy the lease must be compared with. The question is whether leases reach the main line's latency without the 4 GiB of host RAM (compare server_rss_peak_mb in sweep.csv). W1 tool waits are 0.5-2 s, so every hold-max-s >= 2 behaves the same here. Compare with: python -m analysis.paired results/phase2_lease --baseline fifo_c5; and against the main line with --baseline fifo_c6_p5_cram4g.",
